  "summary": "A pig launcher is the pipeline trap used to insert a \"pig\" — a cleaning, gauging or inspection device — into a flowing pipeline. The pig is loaded through the closure door into the oversize barrel; after closing and pressurising, the kicker line and valves are lined up so the flow pushes the pig through the reducer into the pipeline.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Pipeline equipment",
    "type": "Horizontal pig launching trap"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "sequence": "Isolate → depressurise & drain → open door → load pig → close → fill & vent → pressurise → open trap valve → open kicker → close mainline valve → pig launched",
    "safety": "Pressure-warning lock prevents opening the door under pressure"
  },
